        "raw": "<p>A quick question I had, one with probably a simple ruling, but I&#39;d be interested to hear what you guys have to say/think:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&quot;Indestructible: If a card is indestructible, it cannot be destroyed or removed from play.&quot;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&quot;Sky-Scraper Gameplay: [...] start the game with her normal character card in play and the other two character cards off to the side - neither in play nor in hand. Whenever you play a card with a size keyword, switch her character card to the size named on the played card&quot;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So lets say Fixed point is in play with Skyscraper. Her character card are now indestructible meaning it cannot be removed from play. So, if a new size keyword is played what happens? Could she simultaniously tiny and huge? Or would she stay in her size are you are unable to complete the switch? Or are her character cards and exception, the same way one-shots are (to my understanding)?</p>",
